  "question": "The corner points of the feasible region determined by the system of linear constraints are (0, 0), (0, 40), (20, 40) (60, 20) and (60, 0). If the objective function of an LPP is $Z=4x+3y$, then the maximum value is:",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "**Step 1:** Evaluate $Z=4x+3y$ at each corner point.<br />**Step 2:** At (0,0), Z = 0.<br />**Step 3:** At (0,40), Z = $4(0)+3(40)=120$.<br />**Step 4:** At (20,40), Z = $4(20)+3(40) = 80+120=200$.<br />**Step 5:** At (60,20), Z = $4(60)+3(20) = 240+60=300$.<br />**Step 6:** At (60,0), Z = $4(60)+3(0)=240$.<br />**Step 7:** The maximum value is 300.",
